<title>PORTUGAL: Morris says too early to think of Tabacalera.</title>
<headline>Morris says too early to think of Tabacalera.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. tobacco giant Philip Morris, which has just won its bid to buy 65 percent of Portuguese state-owned tobacco concern Tabaqueira, said it was too early to think about the privatisation of Spain's Tabacalera.</p>
<p>Addressing a news conference in Lisbon, the president of Philip Morris Europe said: &quot;It is far too early to speculate. There have been rumours and reports in the last five years about its privatisation. When it happens, we'll see.&quot;</p>
<p>Tabacalera's financial director told Reuters recently that the Spanish government might sell off its 52 percent stake in the company in late 1997 or early 1998.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
